export anchor TelegramStyle:
    number: 120
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Telegram
    idea: The dashboard is a telegram form, with printed brown field labels and boxes and every fact pasted on as an uppercase teletype tape strip closed with STOP.
    base: light
    palette:
        counter: #dcdcd2, the page behind the form
        formBuff: #f4ecd2, the form and the style sheet
        formPrint: #8a2f1d, labels, rules, frames, the primary button, this week and focus
        tape: #fffcf0, pasted strips that carry all data
        ink: #1f1c17, teletype text
        muted: #5c5345, STOP separators and placeholders
        okGreen: #2b5e2b, the On track code with a dot
        riskBrown: #7f4500, the dashed At risk code with a triangle
        lateRed: #9b1c1c, the heavy Behind code with a square and overdue text
        focusYellow: #fff3b8, the fill behind focused controls
    type:
        Three stacks. Teletype is Lucida Console, Andale Mono, DejaVu Sans
        Mono, Liberation Mono, Monaco, monospace, always uppercase on tape.
        Slab is Rockwell, Roboto Slab, Clarendon, Century Schoolbook, Bookman
        Old Style, Georgia, serif for the masthead. Narrow is Arial Narrow,
        Liberation Sans Narrow, Roboto Condensed, Arial, sans-serif for
        printed labels. Sizes are 34px bold slab caps masthead, 30px bold
        teletype figures, 20px teletype greeting, 13 to 15px teletype data
        and 10 to 12px bold narrow caps labels with 0.12em tracking.
    layout:
        One buff form framed by a printed 2px line and a 1px line inside it.
        The masthead has a round lightning bolt seal, the brand in brown
        slab caps with Telegraph, team wires under it, and three boxed
        fields on the right for No. 1031, Filed 31 OCT 26 and Day SAT, over
        a double rule. A service row labelled Check service desired holds
        the navigation as printed checkboxes, the current one crossed with
        an X and underlined, and on the right a labelled Query field, a
        brown New project button, a bell with its count and a To field with
        the user. The Message area pastes three tape strips, the greeting,
        the date and a red urgent strip, each ending in STOP. Four boxed
        fields each hold one figure on tape. Project wires is a ruled grid
        with a number column, and every cell is a tape strip, the name and
        team joined by STOP, a text bar such as seven hashes and three
        dashes in brackets with 72 pct, tasks, due date and a status code.
        The chart is a tape ticker in a pre block, one line per day with
        hashes for the count, last week in ink with its total and this week
        in brown with its total. Incoming wires lists activity as tape
        strips. Below 1000px each project row stacks its cells under the
        number.
    spacing: An 8px unit. The form inset 30px inside the double frame, 9px row padding and 28px before sections.
    density: Dense like a form. Data in columns of printed boxes, one wire per project.
    corners: Square everywhere. No rounding at all.
    borders: 1px form print rules, a 3px double rule under the masthead, and a 2px plus 1px frame round the form.
    shadows: Only the tape strips lift, with a 1px shadow like glued paper, and the form has a soft drop.
    icons:
        Few. A lightning bolt seal. Status codes pair the caps word with a
        filled dot, a triangle or a square in a 1.5px, dashed or 3px frame.
        Overdue is red tape text. Nav uses printed checkboxes.
    focus: A 3px form print outline offset 2px over a pale yellow fill.
    tone: Clipped wire language in caps, ending phrases with STOP, such as Good morning Mara STOP.
